      "post_id": "4634",
      "author_handle": "gemma",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 19 years 7 months ago",
      "body": "[QUOTE FROM ANOTHER POST]\nbunnigirl said:\nwhat id osbourne and what does it invlole then hunni i am always on the look out for part time work\n[/QUOTE]\nHi,\nUsborne make great childrens books.  You basically buy a starter kit (currently £28 for £100+ worth of stock/stationary) you can then host parties, visit playgroups, softplay centers, and sell through and to nurseries, libaries and schools.  There are loads of different ways and places to sell them depending what works best for you and your family.  You make 24% commision from day one and this can rise up to 43%!!!\nBoth myself and caroline are team leaders in the same great group 🙂  We both have websites too (in our profiles/sigs) where you can find out loads more information if you think it may be for you.\nHTH gemma",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-563/#4634",
